			</item>
		<item>
		<title>Russian terrorist attack targets Ukrainian energy grid: two workers killed, thousands left without power as winter nears</title>
		<link>https://euromaidanpress.com/2025/10/11/russian-terrorist-attack-targets-ukrainian-energy-grid-two-workers-killed-thousands-left-without-power-as-winter-nears/</link>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Vira Kravchuk]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Sat, 11 Oct 2025 09:04:50 +0000</pubDate>
				<category><![CDATA[Latest news Ukraine]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[attacks on energy grid]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[civilian casualties]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[double-tap tactic]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[main]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[power outages]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Russian attacks on civilians in Ukraine]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Russian terror]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://euromaidanpress.com/?p=365959</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[On the night of 11 October, Russian forces used a double-strike tactic to attack energy workers and firefighters who came to extinguish fires. ]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[<p><img width="1024" height="682" src="https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/2025-10-11-10.38.15-1024x682.jpg" class="attachment-large size-large wp-post-image" alt="Firefighter responds to fire in Odesa after Russian drone attack, 11 October 2025." decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/2025-10-11-10.38.15-1024x682.jpg 1024w, https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/2025-10-11-10.38.15-300x200.jpg 300w, https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/2025-10-11-10.38.15-380x253.jpg 380w, https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/2025-10-11-10.38.15-800x533.jpg 800w, https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/2025-10-11-10.38.15-1160x773.jpg 1160w, https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/2025-10-11-10.38.15.jpg 1280w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" /></p><div data-type="_mgwidget" data-widget-id="1845881"></div>        
        <script>
            (function(w,q){w[q]=w[q]||[];w[q].push(["_mgc.load"])})(window,"_mgq");
        </script>
    
<p>Russian drones didn't just hit <strong>Ukraine's power grid</strong> on the night of 10-11 October—they waited and struck again, using the double-strike tactic and targeting the firefighters and repair crews who rushed to help.</p>



<p>Near Zhadove in northeastern <strong>Chernihiv Oblast,</strong> a Russian drone hit a utility vehicle belonging to the regional energy company around 10:20 p.m. The vehicle caught fire.</p>



<p>As workers responded to extinguish the flames, a second drone struck another company vehicle. <strong>Two energy workers died</strong> in the attacks, with three others injured, according to the <a href="https://t.me/dsns_telegram/51066">State emergency service. </a></p>



<p>The pattern repeated when local firefighters arrived. Russian forces attacked the fire team as they worked, damaging a fire truck. No firefighters were injured in that strike.</p>



<div class="pk-content-block pk-block-shadows">The overnight attacks fit a documented pattern of <a href="https://euromaidanpress.com/2025/10/10/russias-strikes-on-civilians-are-terrorism-were-calling-them-that/">Russian terrorist strikes</a> against Ukrainian civilians and critical infrastructure.<br><br>Russia systematically targets <strong>Ukraine's energy infrastructure</strong> before winter to deprive civilians of heating, electricity, and water as temperatures drop—a strategy designed to break public morale and force Ukraine toward surrender. <br><br>These attacks cause widespread <strong>blackouts</strong> affecting millions, disrupt military logistics, and force Ukraine to rely on expensive energy imports. </div>



<blockquote class="twitter-tweet"><p>Russian forces killed two energy workers in Chernihiv Oblast using double-strike tactics—hitting their vehicle with a drone, then attacking again as colleagues tried to rescue them.<br><br>One severely wounded worker later died in hospital, bringing the death toll to two, with three… <a href="https://t.co/oyJ2XuSZW2">pic.twitter.com/oyJ2XuSZW2</a></p>— Euromaidan Press (@EuromaidanPress) <a href="https://twitter.com/EuromaidanPress/status/1976926501544120736?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw">October 11, 2025</a></blockquote> <script async src="https://platform.twitter.com/widgets.js"></script>



<p><strong>[UPDATE: Ministry of Energy identifies victims]</strong></p><div data-fuse="incontent_1"></div>



<p>The Ministry of Energy of Ukraine <a href="https://mev.gov.ua/novyna/vnaslidok-vorozhoyi-ataky-na-chernihivshchyni-zahynuly-dvoye-enerhetykiv">identified</a> the two victims as Anatolii Savchenko, 46, a crane operator-driver, and Ruslan Deineha, 47, a driver, both employees of Chernihivoblenergo.</p>



<p>The energy workers' brigade was returning from restoration work on the evening of 10 October when Russian forces attacked them with strike drones, likely Lancet-type models. Savchenko died at the scene. After the first explosion, when colleagues rushed to help their severely wounded teammate, Russian forces delivered a second targeted strike. Deyneha died from his wounds in hospital despite doctors' efforts.</p>



<p>The Ministry characterized the double-strike tactic as "a deliberate war crime aimed at killing civilian specialists—energy workers." Three other colleagues remain hospitalized receiving medical care.</p>



<figure><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1024" height="576" src="https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/Savchenko-Anatolii-1024x576.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-366028" srcset="https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/Savchenko-Anatolii-1024x576.jpg 1024w, https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/Savchenko-Anatolii-300x169.jpg 300w, https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/Savchenko-Anatolii-380x214.jpg 380w, https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/Savchenko-Anatolii-800x450.jpg 800w, https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/Savchenko-Anatolii-1160x653.jpg 1160w, https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/Savchenko-Anatolii.jpg 1280w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" /></figure>



<h3 id="russia-launches-78-drones-on-11-october-night" class="wp-block-heading">Russia launches 78 drones on 11 October night</h3>



<p>Russian forces <a href="https://t.me/kpszsu/44420">launched</a> <strong>78 strike drones</strong>, including approximately 40 Shahed-type unmanned aerial vehicles along with "Gerbera" and other drone models.</p>



<p>Ukrainian air defense forces <strong>neutralized 54</strong> of the incoming threats using electronic warfare units, drone systems, and mobile fire groups.</p>



<p>By 9:00 a.m., 21 drones had struck six separate locations across northern, southern, and eastern Ukraine.</p>



<p>The assault targeted energy infrastructure critical for heating and survival in the months ahead, causing widespread damage and civilian casualties.</p><div data-fuse="incontent_2"></div>



<h3 id="odesa-loses-power-woman-injured" class="wp-block-heading">Odesa loses power, woman injured</h3>



<p>In southern Odesa Oblast, the strikes damaged electrical equipment, two residential buildings, and a hotel complex. A three-story hotel-restaurant complex caught fire, along with energy infrastructure facilities. Firefighters rescued two people while extinguishing the blaze.</p>



<figure class="wp-block-gallery-2 is-layout-flex wp-block-gallery-is-layout-flex">

<figure><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1024" height="682" data-id="365969" src="https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/2025-10-11-10.38.05-1024x682.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-365969" srcset="https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/2025-10-11-10.38.05-1024x682.jpg 1024w, https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/2025-10-11-10.38.05-300x200.jpg 300w, https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/2025-10-11-10.38.05-380x253.jpg 380w, https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/2025-10-11-10.38.05-800x533.jpg 800w, https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/2025-10-11-10.38.05-1160x773.jpg 1160w, https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/2025-10-11-10.38.05.jpg 1280w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" /></figure>


<figure><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1024" height="682" data-id="365970" src="https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/2025-10-11-10.38.10-1024x682.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-365970" srcset="https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/2025-10-11-10.38.10-1024x682.jpg 1024w, https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/2025-10-11-10.38.10-300x200.jpg 300w, https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/2025-10-11-10.38.10-380x253.jpg 380w, https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/2025-10-11-10.38.10-800x533.jpg 800w, https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/2025-10-11-10.38.10-1160x773.jpg 1160w, https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/2025-10-11-10.38.10.jpg 1280w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" /></figure>

</figure>



<figure><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1024" height="684" src="https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/2025-10-11-10.38.21-1-1024x684.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-365973" srcset="https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/2025-10-11-10.38.21-1-1024x684.jpg 1024w, https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/2025-10-11-10.38.21-1-300x200.jpg 300w, https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/2025-10-11-10.38.21-1-380x254.jpg 380w, https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/2025-10-11-10.38.21-1-800x534.jpg 800w, https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/2025-10-11-10.38.21-1-1160x775.jpg 1160w, https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/2025-10-11-10.38.21-1.jpg 1280w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" /><figcaption>The terrorist Russian attack on energy and civilian infrastructure left 44 settlements without power and one woman hospitalized in Odesa on 11 October. Photos: State emergency service (SES)</figcaption></figure>



<p>The attack <strong><a href="https://suspilne.media/odesa/1136308-rf-masovano-atakuvav-odesu-ta-oblast-prokuratura-fiksue-naslidki-obstrilu/">left</a> 44 settlements without electricity.</strong> A 25-story residential building lost the glazing on one floor. Two private houses sustained damage.</p>



<p>A 47-year-old woman was hospitalized with injuries. Parts of Odesa city and the surrounding district remained without power.</p>



<figure><div class="wp-block-embed__wrapper">
<blockquote class="twitter-tweet" data-width="550" data-dnt="true"><p lang="en" dir="ltr">Russian terrorist attacks on power grid in Odesa left 44 settlements without electricity on the night of 11 October.<br><br>Russia targets Ukraine's energy infrastructure ahead of winter to deprive Ukrainians of essential heating, power, and water as temperatures drop. <br><br>The drone… <a href="https://t.co/fH2BOYgeej">pic.twitter.com/fH2BOYgeej</a></p>— Euromaidan Press (@EuromaidanPress) <a href="https://twitter.com/EuromaidanPress/status/1976920780412801425?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw">October 11, 2025</a></blockquote><script async src="https://platform.twitter.com/widgets.js" charset="utf-8"></script>
</div></figure>



<figure class="wp-block-gallery-3 is-layout-flex wp-block-gallery-is-layout-flex">

<figure><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="851" height="1024" data-id="365979" src="https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/2025-10-11-10.37.30-851x1024.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-365979" srcset="https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/2025-10-11-10.37.30-851x1024.jpg 851w, https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/2025-10-11-10.37.30-249x300.jpg 249w, https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/2025-10-11-10.37.30-380x457.jpg 380w, https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/2025-10-11-10.37.30-800x962.jpg 800w, https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/2025-10-11-10.37.30.jpg 1064w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 851px) 100vw, 851px" /></figure>


<figure><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1024" height="765" data-id="365975" src="https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/2025-10-11-10.37.32-1024x765.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-365975" srcset="https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/2025-10-11-10.37.32-1024x765.jpg 1024w, https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/2025-10-11-10.37.32-300x225.jpg 300w, https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/2025-10-11-10.37.32-200x150.jpg 200w, https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/2025-10-11-10.37.32-260x195.jpg 260w, https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/2025-10-11-10.37.32-380x284.jpg 380w, https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/2025-10-11-10.37.32-800x598.jpg 800w, https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/2025-10-11-10.37.32-1160x866.jpg 1160w, https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/2025-10-11-10.37.32.jpg 1280w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" /><figcaption>Aftermath of the Russian attack on civilian infrastructure in Odesa, 11 October.</figcaption></figure>


<figure><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1024" height="765" data-id="365977" src="https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/2025-10-11-10.37.35-1024x765.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-365977" srcset="https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/2025-10-11-10.37.35-1024x765.jpg 1024w, https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/2025-10-11-10.37.35-300x225.jpg 300w, https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/2025-10-11-10.37.35-200x150.jpg 200w, https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/2025-10-11-10.37.35-260x195.jpg 260w, https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/2025-10-11-10.37.35-380x284.jpg 380w, https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/2025-10-11-10.37.35-800x598.jpg 800w, https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/2025-10-11-10.37.35-1160x866.jpg 1160w, https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/2025-10-11-10.37.35.jpg 1280w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" /><figcaption>Photos: Prosecutor's Office</figcaption></figure>

</figure>



<h3 id="more-strikes-hit-chernihiv-infrastructure" class="wp-block-heading">More strikes hit Chernihiv infrastructure</h3><div data-fuse="incontent_3"></div>



<p>Beyond the deadly attack on energy workers, Russian drones struck infrastructure facilities in Nizhyn district, causing fires that rescuers quickly extinguished.</p>



<p>In Novhorod-Siverskyi, a drone hit a building and ignited a blaze consuming 160 square meters before firefighters brought it under control.</p>



<h3 id="kherson-ambulance-struck-child-wounded" class="wp-block-heading">Kherson ambulance struck, child wounded</h3>



<p>In southern Kherson Oblast, <strong>four people were wounded,</strong> including a child.</p>



<p>A 59-year-old <strong>ambulance</strong> driver sustained injuries when Russian forces dropped explosives from a drone onto the emergency medical vehicle.</p>



<p>Overnight strikes on eastern Kharkiv Oblast targeted Chuhuiv city and Velykyi Burluk village in Kupiansk district. The drone impacts caused destruction and fires, with preliminary reports indicating <strong>one person injured.</strong></p>


