		<item>
		<title>Ukraine&#8217;s FM calls Russia &#8220;worse than Hamas&#8221; as 465 drones strike energy grid on attack anniversary</title>
		<link>https://euromaidanpress.com/2025/10/10/ukraines-fm-calls-russia-worse-than-hamas-as-465-drones-strike-energy-grid-on-attack-anniversary/</link>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Maxim Volovich]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Fri, 10 Oct 2025 18:51:40 +0000</pubDate>
				<category><![CDATA[Latest news Ukraine]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Russian Aggression]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Russian War Crimes]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Andrii Sybiha]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[civilian casualties]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[energy war]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[genocide convention]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[October 10 attack]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Russia attacks Ukraine]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Russian aggression]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Russian drones]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Russian terrorism]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Ukraine diplomacy]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Ukraine energy infrastructure]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Ukraine winter]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[war crimes]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://euromaidanpress.com/?p=365791</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[Sybiha: Even Hamas agreed to ceasefire talks, Moscow rejects all diplomacy]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[<p><img width="1024" height="717" src="https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/russia-worse-than-hamas-sybiha-ukraine-energy-attacks-1024x717.jpeg" class="attachment-large size-large wp-post-image" alt="Ukraine’s FM Sybiha: “Russia is worse than Hamas” after 465-drone strike cripples energy grid" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/russia-worse-than-hamas-sybiha-ukraine-energy-attacks-1024x717.jpeg 1024w, https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/russia-worse-than-hamas-sybiha-ukraine-energy-attacks-300x210.jpeg 300w, https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/russia-worse-than-hamas-sybiha-ukraine-energy-attacks-380x266.jpeg 380w, https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/russia-worse-than-hamas-sybiha-ukraine-energy-attacks-800x560.jpeg 800w, https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/russia-worse-than-hamas-sybiha-ukraine-energy-attacks-1160x812.jpeg 1160w, https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/russia-worse-than-hamas-sybiha-ukraine-energy-attacks.jpeg 1280w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" /></p><div data-type="_mgwidget" data-widget-id="1845881"></div>        
        <script>
            (function(w,q){w[q]=w[q]||[];w[q].push(["_mgc.load"])})(window,"_mgq");
        </script>
    
<p>Ukrainian Foreign Minister Andrii Sybiha <a href="https://x.com/andrii_sybiha/status/1976524891705745828">declared</a> Russia "worse than Hamas" on 10 October 2025, hours after Moscow launched 465 drones and 32 missiles against civilian and energy infrastructure across Ukraine.</p>



<pre class="wp-block-preformatted">The attack killed a 7-year-old boy in Zaporizhzhia and left tens of thousands without power as Russia intensifies its pre-winter assault on heating infrastructure—a campaign that has <a href="https://euromaidanpress.com/2025/10/09/russia-destroys-60-of-ukraines-gas-production-weeks-before-winter-heating-season/">destroyed 60% of Ukraine's gas production</a> in recent weeks and left the country operating at only 40% of pre-war electricity capacity.</pre>



<h3 id="why-russia-is-worse-than-hamas" class="wp-block-heading">Why Russia is "worse than Hamas"</h3>



<blockquote class="wp-block-quote is-layout-flow wp-block-quote-is-layout-flow">
<p>"Russia is worse than Hamas. Even Hamas has agreed to a ceasefire and peace efforts. To the contrary, Moscow continues the senseless war it began—the war it cannot and will not win," Sybiha wrote on X.</p>
</blockquote><div data-fuse="incontent_1"></div>



<p>The foreign minister pointed to Moscow's three-year pattern of "aggressive actions, terrorist methods, and ultimatums" while rejecting "any meaningful diplomacy and peace efforts." The timing itself carried symbolism reminiscent of the Kremlin’s taste for dark anniversaries: Russia <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Russian_strikes_against_Ukrainian_infrastructure_(2022%E2%80%93present)">launched</a> its first massive energy attack on 10 October 2022, using 84 cruise missiles and 24 drones that damaged 30% of Ukraine's power grid.</p>



<h3 id="overnight-barrage-cripples-multiple-regions" class="wp-block-heading">Overnight barrage cripples multiple regions</h3>



<p>The latest strike injured dozens across nine regions while cutting power to Kyiv, Kharkiv, Poltava, Zaporizhzhia, and Dnipro. Ukrainian air defenses intercepted 405 drones and 15 missiles, but significant damage occurred to energy facilities.</p>



<p>Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelenskyy <a href="https://x.com/ZelenskyyUa/status/1976533716202590557">called</a> it "a cynical and calculated attack, with more than 450 drones and over 30 missiles targeting everything that sustains normal life." Prime Minister Yuliia Svyrydenko described it as one of the largest concentrated strikes against Ukraine's energy infrastructure since the invasion began.</p>



<h3 id="three-year-pattern-of-winter-energy-warfare" class="wp-block-heading">Three-year pattern of winter energy warfare</h3><div data-fuse="incontent_2"></div>



<p>The 10 October 2022 attack killed 14 people, injured 97, and triggered rolling blackouts that marked the start of Russia's winter energy campaign. Each subsequent cold season has brought intensified strikes, leaving even major cities such as Kyiv and Kharkiv facing substantial electricity shortages.</p>



<p>The cumulative damage now threatens Ukraine's ability to heat homes as temperatures drop. Recent strikes knocked out nearly 60% of gas production capacity, forcing Kyiv to secure €1.9 billion in emergency loans for winter fuel imports.</p>



<h3 id="genocide-under-article-ii-c" class="wp-block-heading">"Genocide under Article II (c)"</h3>



<blockquote class="wp-block-quote is-layout-flow wp-block-quote-is-layout-flow">
<p>"Depriving people of energy amid dropping autumn temperatures amounts to genocide under Article II (c) of the Genocide Convention: creating unbearable conditions of life in order to destroy a national group," Sybiha argued.</p>
</blockquote>



<p>He praised Ukrainian energy workers as "true heroes" restoring power under fire, but stressed the country needs increased international energy assistance to survive the winter.</p><div data-fuse="incontent_3"></div>



<h3 id="three-pronged-pressure-strategy" class="wp-block-heading">Three-pronged pressure strategy</h3>



<p>Sybiha outlined his response framework: "Economic pressure of biting sanctions, military pressure of stronger support for Ukraine, and political pressure of full isolation."</p>



<blockquote class="wp-block-quote is-layout-flow wp-block-quote-is-layout-flow">
<p>"Putin must feel that the cost of continuing the war exceeds the cost of stopping it. He must feel that continuing this war endangers his regime," the foreign minister stated.</p>
</blockquote>



<h3 id="related" class="wp-block-heading">Related:</h3>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li><a href="https://euromaidanpress.com/2025/10/09/russia-destroys-60-of-ukraines-gas-production-weeks-before-winter-heating-season/">Russia destroys 60% of Ukraine's gas production weeks before winter heating season</a></li>



<li><a href="https://euromaidanpress.com/2025/10/05/putin-mocks-the-wests-silence-zelenskyy/">Putin mocks the West's silence as Russia bombards Ukraine with Western-made components - Zelenskyy</a></li>
</ul>



<p></p>

